oad() != 1 {\n   146\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"the pending key was computed again across the bound: %d after %d calls\", v, calls.Load())\n   147\t\t}\n   148\t}\nrecurrence.flapping_keys=0\nrecurrence.resolved_clusters=0\nrecurrence.window_days=14\nrecurrence.threshold=3\nrecurrence.records_scanned=432\nrecurrence.flagged_keys=0\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_24","type":"agent_message","text":"I found one remaining R5 defect: pending entries can all become retained values without another capacity check. With a bound of one, the existing capacity-crossing test leaves both A and B retained; an arbitrarily large burst of distinct pending keys can leave the same number cached until a later miss.\n\nThe prior findings are fixed. The focused race tests passed, including 100 repetitions of the three concurrent-miss tests, and the surface check reported no findings."}}
